{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"find /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1030756833/13 -maxdepth 2 -type f -print -exec sed -n '1,200p' {} \\\\;\"","aggregated_output":"/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1030756833/13/ids.txt\ntrain/9f669b64\ntrain/bc93ec48\ntrain/5a719d11\ntrain/58c02a16\ntrain/54dc2872\ntrain/3cd86f4f\ntrain/9841fdad\ntrain/880c1354\ntrain/78e78cff\neval/4a21e3da\neval/b9e38dc0\ntrain/ecb67b6d\ntrain/14b8e18c\ntrain/825aa9e9\ntrain/9968a131\neval/cb2d8a2c\neval/9385bd28\ntrain/9720b24f\ntrain/d93c6891\ntrain/ad173014\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1030756833/13/des.md\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：根据每个封闭区域内标记像素的颜色，在该区域的边框上找到同色缺口，并从缺口向外延伸射线直到碰到其他物体或网格边缘，射线颜色取自区域内标记像素的颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干由 Grey 像素构成的封闭矩形边框（边框宽度为一个像素）。\n  - 每个矩形边框上恰好有一个缺口（缺口宽度为一个像素，即边框某条边上缺少一个 Grey 像素）。\n  - 每个封闭矩形内部恰好有一个非背景色的单像素标记（颜色可以是 Red、Blue、Green、Yellow 等，各矩形标记颜色可能不同）。\n  - 矩形之间不重叠，但可能在同一行或同一列上。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保持所有输入内容不变。\n  - 对每个 Grey 矩形边框，找到其缺口位置，确定缺口朝向（上、下、左、右）。\n  - 读取该矩形内部标记像素的颜色。\n  - 从缺口位置沿缺口朝外的方向延伸一条该标记颜色的射线（逐像素绘制），直到碰到另一个 Grey 像素、另一条已绘制的射线或网格边缘为止（不覆盖碰到的那个像素）。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 缺口的位置决定射线的方向，而内部标记的颜色决定射线的颜色——解题者需要同时关联两个独立线索（缺口方位与内部颜色）才能确定每条射线的完整参数。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：将网格中散落的彩色碎片按颜色配对，每对碎片沿它们连线的中点进行 180 度旋转合并，拼合后的完整图形用第三种颜色（由图例行指定）重新着色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格最底部一行是图例行：包含若干颜色对，每对由两个相邻像素组成——左像素是碎片颜色，右像素是该碎片配对合并后应重新着色的目标颜色。图例对之间用一个 Black 像素分隔。\n  - 网格其余区域散布着若干单色 4-连通碎片。每种碎片颜色恰好出现两个碎片，且两个碎片的形状互为 180 度旋转关系。\n  - 同色的两个碎片若将其中一个绕两者边界框联合中心旋转 180 度，则恰好与另一个碎片无重叠地拼合成一个完整的矩形。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 在图例行中读取每种碎片颜色对应的目标颜色。\n  - 对每对同色碎片，计算两者边界框的联合中心（联合边界框的几何中心）。\n  - 将其中一个碎片绕该联合中心旋转 180 度，使其与另一个碎片拼合。\n  - 将拼合后的完整矩形全部像素重新着色为图例指定的目标颜色。\n  - 清除碎片原来位置上不再被覆盖的像素（恢复为背景色）。\n  - 图例行在输出中保留不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 解题者需要先从图例行建立颜色映射关系，再识别出同色碎片的互补旋转关系并找到正确的合并位置——这是两层独立的非显然推理：配色映射与空间旋转拼合。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：每个彩色对象根据其内部孔洞的数量，在网格中对应行号的水平参考线上留下该对象颜色的标记条，标记条的宽度等于对象本身的宽度。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格左侧有一列由 Maroon 像素构成的竖直参考轴（占据第 0 列，从第 0 行到最后一行）。\n  - 网格中散布若干不同颜色的 4-连通前景对象，每个对象是封闭的形状，内部可能包含零个或多个由背景色构成的孔洞（孔洞定义为被该对象像素完全包围的背景色 4-连通区域）。\n  - 每个对象的颜色互不相同。\n  - 对象不接触参考轴，也不接触网格边缘。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保持所有输入内容不变（对象、参考轴、背景）。\n  - 对每个前景对象，数出其内部孔洞的数量 N（N 范围为 0 到 5）。\n  - 在参考轴上，从第 N 行开始（第 0 行为参考轴最顶端），沿该行向右绘制一条水平标记条。标记条颜色为该对象的颜色，长度（像素数）等于该对象边界框的宽度。标记条从第 1 列开始绘制（紧贴参考轴右侧）。\n  - 如果多个对象具有相同的孔洞数量，则它们的标记条绘制在同一行上，按对象边界框左边缘的列号从小到大排列，依次紧挨放置。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 孔洞数量是对象的隐含拓扑属性，解题者必须先识别\"孔洞计数决定行位置\"这一非显然映射，再理解\"对象宽度决定标记条长度\"这一第二层规则——两层推理缺一不可。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中的彩色箭头指向相邻的灰色容器，容器内部需要被填充为箭头的颜色，但填充图案是箭头自身形状去掉箭杆后的箭头尖端形状的平铺。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中有若干 Grey 像素构成的矩形空心容器（边框宽一个像素，内部全为背景色）。\n  - 每个容器的某一侧外部紧贴着一个彩色箭头。箭头由箭杆和箭头尖端组成：箭杆是一条直线段（宽一个像素，长度至少两个像素），箭头尖端是箭杆末端的一个三角形（由三个像素组成的 V 形：箭杆方向的前端一个像素加上垂直于箭杆方向的两侧各一个像素）。箭头方向指向容器（即箭头尖端朝向容器那一侧的边框）。\n  - 每个容器最多只有一个箭头指向它。没有箭头指向的容器保持不变。\n  - 不同箭头使用不同颜色（Red、Blue、Green、Yellow、Orange 等）。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保持所有 Grey 边框和箭头不变。\n  - 对每个被箭头指向的容器：\n    - 提取箭头尖端的形状（三个像素的 V 形图案）。\n    - 将这个 V 形图案作为瓷砖，以箭头颜色从容器内部左上角开始逐行逐列平铺填充容器内部空间。平铺时瓷砖之间无间隔，超出容器内部边界的部分裁剪掉。\n  - 没有箭头的容器内部保持为背景色。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 解题者不仅要识别箭头与容器的配对关系和颜色传递，还需要发现填充图案并非简单的纯色填充，而是箭头尖端形状的重复平铺——箭头同时编码了颜色和图案两重信息。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格被分为左右两个面板，左面板包含若干带有颜色标签的形状模板，右面板包含同样数量的灰色目标区域；每个目标区域需要被填充为与其面积相同的那个模板的形状，并着上模板标签的颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 一条竖直的 Maroon 分隔线将网格等分为左右两个面板。\n  - 左面板中有若干用 Grey 像素绘制的形状模板（4-连通区域），每个模板内部恰好嵌入一个不同颜色的单像素标签（如 Red、Blue、Green 等），标签位于模板形状内部任意位置。\n  - 右面板中有若干用 Grey 像素填充的实心矩形目标区域，每个目标区域的面积（像素总数）恰好等于左面板中某一个模板的面积（Grey 像素数加上标签像素数）。\n  - 左面板模板的面积两两不同，因此面积匹配是唯一的。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 分隔线保持不变。\n  - 对右面板中的每个灰色目标矩形：\n    - 计算其面积（像素数）。\n    - 在左面板中找到面积相同的模板。\n    - 读取该模板内嵌标签的颜色。\n    - 将模板的形状（包含标签位置在内的完整形状）绘制在目标矩形的左上角对齐位置，使用标签颜色绘制整个形状。\n    - 目标矩形中未被模板形状覆盖的像素恢复为背景色。\n  - 左面板保持不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 解题者需要通过面积匹配来建立左右面板的对应关系——这要求先数出各区域的像素数量进行配对，再把模板形状按标签颜色\"印\"到右侧，涉及\"面积配对\"和\"形状转移+重着色\"两层独立推理。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：识别网格中由不同颜色线段围成的封闭多边形区域，按照每个多边形边数的奇偶性选择不同的填充策略：奇数边用边框颜色中出现最多的那种颜色填充内部，偶数边则将内部所有背景像素替换为该多边形独有的（未在其他多边形边框中出现的）边框颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Azure。\n  - 网格中有若干封闭多边形，每个多边形的边框由直线段组成，线段宽度为一个像素。\n  - 每条边是一段水平或竖直的直线段，每条边可以有不同的颜色（使用 Red、Green、Blue、Yellow、Orange 等）。\n  - 多边形的顶点处两条边共享一个角像素。多边形之间不共享边或顶点，不嵌套、不重叠。\n  - 每个多边形的边数在 3 到 6 之间（由直角转弯处分隔确定边数）。\n  - 每个多边形内部全为背景色。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保持所有边框像素不变。\n  - 对每个封闭多边形：\n    - 数出其边数 E（通过数角点数量确定，角点即边框上方向发生 90 度转变的像素）。\n    - 如果 E 为奇数：统计该多边形所有边框像素中各颜色的出现次数，取出现次数最多的颜色，将多边形内部背景像素全部填充为该颜色。\n    - 如果 E 为偶数：找出该多边形边框中使用了但其他所有多边形边框中未使用的颜色（保证恰好存在一种），将多边形内部背景像素全部填充为该独有颜色。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 解题者需要先通过数角点来判断边数的奇偶性（第一层推理），再根据奇偶性选择截然不同的颜色选取策略（第二层推理）——奇数边看\"最多\"，偶数边看\"独有\"，两套逻辑隐藏在同一个变换中。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n<new_puzzle>\n- `description`：网格中散落的单色碎片需要沿着隐含的对称轴镜像翻折，对称轴由网格边缘上成对出现的同色标记像素确定；翻折后碎片与原件重叠的区域变为第三种颜色。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格边缘（第一行、最后一行、第一列、最后一列）上有若干成对的同色标记像素。每对标记颜色相同且恰好出现两个，分布在网格的对边上（如一个在顶边、一个在底边，或一个在左边、一个在右边），且两个标记像素位于同一行或同一列。每对标记定义一条连接它们的直线作为对称轴（水平或竖直）。\n  - 网格内部有若干 4-连通单色前景碎片，每个碎片整体位于某条对称轴的一侧（不跨越对称轴），且碎片颜色与边缘标记颜色均不同。碎片颜色可以相同也可以不同。\n  - 每个碎片恰好只在一条对称轴的一侧。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 保持边缘标记像素不变。\n  - 对每条对称轴，找到位于其一侧的所有碎片。\n  - 将每个碎片沿该对称轴做镜像翻折，在对称位置绘制翻折后的副本（使用碎片原来的颜色）。\n  - 原始碎片保留不变。\n  - 如果翻折后的副本与原始碎片（同一碎片或不同碎片）发生像素重叠，重叠位置的像素变为 Yellow。\n  - 翻折副本不覆盖边缘标记像素。\n\n- `Key insight`：\n  - 解题者首先需要从边缘标记中推断出隐含的对称轴（第一层），再确定每个碎片归属于哪条轴并执行镜像操作（第二层），最后理解重叠区域的特殊着色规则（第三层）——对称轴的存在不直接可见，必须通过边缘标记的位置关系推断。\n</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1030756833/13/prompt.md\n你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9f669b64\" lines=\"26-48\">\n<description>\nPush the central solid rectangle to the grid edge, splitting the perpendicular target rectangle around its path.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly three monochrome foreground objects arranged on one\n  horizontal or vertical axis.\n- The middle object on that axis is a solid rectangular moving object.\n- One end object is a solid rectangle or bar whose long side is perpendicular\n  to the movement axis; this is the target to split.\n\nRule\n- Move the middle rectangle along the axis toward the target until it is\n  flush with the grid edge in that direction.\n- Clear the original middle rectangle and the original target.\n- Split the target through the moving rectangle's two-cell-wide path and\n  shift the two halves one cell outward perpendicular to the movement.\n- Keep the other end object unchanged.\n\nKey insight\n- The non-target end object acts as a pusher; the central rectangle travels\n  away from it through the perpendicular target, opening a matching gap.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"bc93ec48\" lines=\"48-63\">\n<description>\nCopy each foreground object anchored in a true grid corner clockwise into the next corner.\n\nInput structure\n- The dominant color is the background.\n- Foreground objects are monochromatic 4-connected components.\n- Relevant objects are exactly those whose bounding box touches two adjacent borders at one grid corner.\n\nRule\n- Start from the input unchanged.\n- For each corner object, copy its pixel mask and color to the next corner clockwise: top-left to top-right, top-right to bottom-right, bottom-right to bottom-left, and bottom-left to top-left.\n- Preserve each object's orientation by aligning its bounding box to the destination corner; stamps may overwrite existing pixels at the destination, but source pixels are not cleared.\n\nKey insight\n- Interior and side-only objects are distractors; only components actually anchored to a corner participate in the clockwise perimeter copy.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5a719d11\" lines=\"44-59\">\n<description>\nWithin each horizontal pair of two-color panels, swap the motif masks and recolor each pasted mask with the source panel's base color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A separator color forms full blank rows and at least one full blank column.\n- The non-separator area is split into row bands, each containing exactly two same-shaped rectangular panels.\n- Each panel has a dominant base color and one minority motif color.\n\nRule:\n- For every row band, clear each panel to its own base color.\n- Paste the right panel's motif mask into the left panel using the right base color.\n- Paste the left panel's motif mask into the right panel using the left base color.\n\nKey insight:\n- The motif colors themselves are distractors; only each motif's shape mask and the two panel base colors are exchanged.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"58c02a16\" lines=\"10-26\">\n<description>\nExpand the top-left seed mask into a recursive colored pattern and tile it across the full grid.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- All foreground lies in a top-left rectangle whose last row and last column are a solid secondary color.\n- Removing that secondary-color row and column leaves a seed region containing background plus one primary color.\n\nRule\n- Use the primary-color pixels in the seed as a binary mask.\n- Replace each primary seed cell with a copy of the seed mask in the primary color, and each background seed cell\n  with a copy of the seed mask in the secondary color.\n- Repeat and crop that expanded tile to the original grid shape.\n\nKey insight\nThe solid L-shaped secondary-color border is a legend, not output content; it supplies the color used when the\nseed's background cells are expanded.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"54dc2872\" lines=\"52-69\">\n<description>\nMove each marked L-shaped sprite onto the separate pixel matching its marker color.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Foreground has 4-connected multicolor sprites and isolated one-pixel controls.\n- Each sprite has one repeated body color in an L shape plus one embedded marker\n  pixel of a different color.\n\nRule\n- If the embedded marker color also appears as a separate isolated control pixel,\n  translate the whole sprite so the body L-bend lands on that control pixel.\n- Clear each moved sprite from its old position, clear its consumed control pixel,\n  then paste all translated sprites; sprites without a matching control stay put.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker color pairs a sprite with its destination control, while the L-bend\n  gives the orientation-independent anchor cell to place on that destination.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3cd86f4f\" lines=\"6-18\">\n<description>\nShear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.\n\nInput structure\nA rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.\n\nRule\nCreate a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy\neach input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.\n\nKey insight\nThe colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so\nthe left edge forms a descending diagonal.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9841fdad\" lines=\"15-39\">\n<description>\nExpand the colored runs from the left reference panel into the blank right panel.\n\nInput structure:\n- A uniform rectangular frame surrounds the grid.\n- One full-height divider of the frame color splits a left reference panel\n  from a blank right panel.\n- Both panels have one background margin column on each side of their active\n  columns; the left active columns contain two-column endpoint slots, possibly\n  connected by same-color horizontal runs.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the original grid and paint only in the right panel's active columns.\n- A source run exactly matching the left endpoint slot is copied to the left\n  two columns of the right active span.\n- A source run exactly matching the right endpoint slot is copied to the right\n  two columns of the right active span.\n- A source run connecting the endpoint slots is stretched across the entire\n  right active span.\n\nKey insight:\nThe left panel is a compressed legend for the right panel: endpoint markers\nstay two pixels wide, while connectors between endpoints expand to fill the\ndistance between them.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"880c1354\" lines=\"14-28\">\n<description>\nRecolor the separated outer regions by rotating their colors one step clockwise around the yellow-orange divider.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid contains a fixed yellow/orange divider structure.\n- All other colors form separated 4-connected monochrome regions around that divider.\n\nRule:\n- Leave the yellow and orange pixels unchanged.\n- Sort the non-divider regions by their centroid angle around the divider centroid in screen-coordinate clockwise order.\n- Each region keeps its cells and receives the color of the previous region in that cyclic order.\n\nKey insight:\n- The objects do not move; only the color labels cycle through the spatial order of the regions around the divider.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"78e78cff\" lines=\"71-91\">\n<description>\nRecolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\n\nRule:\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\n\nKey insight:\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\n  through connected background.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
